    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "ACS chest pain:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " nitroglycerin is preferable to morphine or fentanyl; use morphine judiciously (eg, nitroglycerin contraindicated or symptoms despite maximal nitroglycerin), given a possible increase in mortality and attenuation of P2Y12 inhibitor activity."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "In ACS:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " can depress respiration, reduce myocardial contractility and is a potent venous vasodilator; hypotension and bradycardia can usually be overcome by prompt elevation of the lower extremities."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Dose (IV):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " 0.1–0.2 mg/kg every 4 hours as needed, at the lowest dose that gives adequate analgesia; inject slowly (rapid IV may cause chest wall rigidity)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Contraindicated:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " significant respiratory depression; MAOI use now or within the last 14 days; known or suspected GI obstruction, including paralytic ileus."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Interactions:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " benzodiazepines or other CNS depressants (including alcohol) may cause profound sedation, respiratory depression, coma and death."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Monitor closely for respiratory depression, especially at the start or after a dose increase; have naloxone and resuscitative equipment immediately available."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Overdose:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " respiratory depression, somnolence progressing to stupor or coma, constricted pupils, bradycardia, hypotension; give naloxone or nalmefene and monitor until spontaneous breathing is reliably back, because reversal is shorter than morphine's action."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
